{"name":"Primula","hex":"#ca9fa5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Primula","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Primulaceae – primroses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Primula"}],"entries":[{"title":"Primula","blocks":[{"text":"Primula is a genus of herbaceous flowering plants in the family Primulaceae. They include the primrose, a familiar wildflower of banks and verges. Other common species are P. auricula (auricula), P. veris (cowslip), and P. elatior (oxlip). These species and many others are valued for their ornamental flowers. They have been extensively cultivated and hybridised. Primula are native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere, south into tropical mountains in Ethiopia, Indonesia, and New Guinea, and in temperate southern South America. Almost half of the known species are from the Himalayas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Prole%C4%87no_cve%C4%87e_3.JPG/330px-Prole%C4%87no_cve%C4%87e_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primula","wikidata":"Q158974"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Primula_algida%2C_%D4%B3%D5%B6%D5%A1%D6%80%D5%A2%D5%B8%D6%82%D5%AF_%D5%BD%D5%A1%D5%BC%D5%A8%2C_%D0%9F%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B2%D0%BE%D1%86%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%82_%D1%85%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Primula_algida%2C_%D4%B3%D5%B6%D5%A1%D6%80%D5%A2%D5%B8%D6%82%D5%AF_%D5%BD%D5%A1%D5%BC%D5%A8%2C_%D0%9F%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B2%D0%BE%D1%86%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%82_%D1%85%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Primula_algida%2C_%D4%B3%D5%B6%D5%A1%D6%80%D5%A2%D5%B8%D6%82%D5%AF_%D5%BD%D5%A1%D5%BC%D5%A8%2C_%D0%9F%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B2%D0%BE%D1%86%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%82_%D1%85%D0%BE%D0%